  <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)]">Cumulative GPA across semesters</h2>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Your cumulative GPA is the average across every term you have completed, weighted by credits. To track it, add
    your courses from each semester into the same list. Because the calculation uses credits, a full-year class counts
    more than a half-credit elective, which mirrors how most transcripts work. Freshmen can see where they stand early,
    while juniors and seniors can estimate their GPA before sending college applications.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)]">Tips for raising your GPA</h2>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Early grades carry the same credit weight as later ones, but they leave less room to recover as time passes. Aim
    to improve in your highest-credit courses first, since they move the average most. Try different grades in the
    calculator to find out how much a single B+ to A change would help. Colleges also look at course rigor, so a
    balanced schedule of challenging classes often matters as much as a perfect 4.0.
  </p>

